    "search": "Use a document request when your firm needs the client to provide specific files or information through the client portal. The request tells the client what is needed, where to provide it, and when it is due. Files uploaded in response remain connected to the request and the client workspace, allowing firm users to track outstanding items without relying on separate email follow-up. Open the client record and select Documents. Select Request. Describe each document or item the client needs to provide. Select the destination folder where the returned files should be stored. Set the due date and complete the recipient and other request details shown in the form. Review the request and confirm that it is being sent to the correct client contact. Send the request. Use the Requests view to monitor outstanding and completed requests. The client receives the request through the client-facing experience and can upload the requested files against it. Once received, the documents remain available in the client's Documents workspace. For example, your firm might request W-2s, 1099s, bank statements, payroll reports, identification documents, or other source documents required for an engagement.",
